UNIT carried_declared
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 f22b9eea6d3d89d34dd82f453c33f79a5960dfe8f916c84e69e917bf852490cc
SIG export function carried_declared(text: string): CarriedDecl | null
ABI TypeScript compiled to the js runtime. Types the artifact declares and exports: type Json = null | boolean | number |
  string | Json[] | { [k: string]: Json }; interface Assertion { expr: string; equals: Json } interface CarriedDecl {
  name: string; from: string; sha: string | null; shape: string | null; assertions: Assertion[] }. text = string (UTF-16;
  every rule is over code points); none = null; json = the value JSON.parse yields, typed Json. STRICT: type-checks under
  strict: true with no any, no non-null assertion (!), no @ts-ignore / @ts-expect-error. A throw is any thrown Error; the
  message is not graded.
MECHANISM (self-contained, as js) SP trims are /^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/g, never trim(). The PINNED charset WS is exactly JS \s;
  the R11 expr test may be /[^\s\p{Cf}]/u only on a host whose Unicode is 17.0 (Node 24) — otherwise spell CF out. In a
  regex without the s flag, . matches neither U+2028 nor U+2029: HEAD's SOURCE refuses them, SUBFIELD and AUTHORITY take them. R11 = JSON.parse on STRING and on E (it returns any: assign it to a Json-typed binding, never widen
  with any); each numeral (after the strings in E are blanked)
  gives X = Number(numeral): throw unless Number.isFinite(X), Math.abs(X) <= 2 ** 53, X is nonzero or the numeral's part
  before e/E has no digit 1-9, and (integer-form only) BigInt(numeral) === BigInt(X).
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex LINES = /\r\n|\r|\n/ CITED R1 — the only line breaks
PINNED regex HEAD = /^([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)[ \t]+FROM[ \t]+(.+)$/ CITED R6 — on ARGS
PINNED regex KEYWORD = /^(?:CANONICAL-SHA256|SHAPE|AUTHORITY)(?![A-Z0-9-])/ CITED R7 — on each BODY: a keyword line, else prose
PINNED regex SUBFIELD = /^(CANONICAL-SHA256|SHAPE|AUTHORITY)(?:[ \t]+([^]*))?$/ CITED R7 — on each keyword line; no match throws; group 2 (or the empty text) is VALUE
PINNED regex AUTHORITY = /^\{[ \t]*expr:[ \t]*("(?:\\[^]|[^"\\])*")[ \t]*,[ \t]*equals:[ \t]*([^]+?)[ \t]*\}$/ CITED R10 — on VALUE; group 1 is STRING, group 2 is E
PINNED regex NUMERAL = /-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?(?:[eE][+-]?\d+)?/g CITED R11 — over E after every JSON string in it is replaced by ""
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/sir/v05.mjs carriedDeclared + cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs, cut by the sighted selfhost decomposer 2026-10-27 (round 5b).
